.TH NFC 1 "November 2026" "New File Creation 2 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nfc \- create files from New File Creation 2 templates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nfc
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B nfc help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B nfc version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nfc
is the command-line companion to New File Creation 2. It creates files from
templates, manages the template library, and inspects the shared configuration
without requiring the app to be running.
.PP
The app, Finder extension, and
.B nfc
all use the same support folder and the same rules for default names and
uniqueness. Existing files are never overwritten.
.PP
The tool is embedded in the app bundle at
.IR "/Applications/New File Creation 2.app/Contents/Helpers/nfc" .
Link it onto
.B PATH
with
.BR "scripts/install-cli.sh" .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options may appear anywhere on the command line.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write exactly one JSON envelope to standard output instead of human text.
.TP
.BR \-\-quiet ", " \-q
Minimal human output. The
.B create
and
.B open
commands print only the path; the
.B add
command prints only added file names.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Accepted for compatibility. Output is already plain and uncolored.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Accepted for compatibility. Output is never colored.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Use
.I path
as the configuration file. Its parent folder becomes the support folder for
.IR config.json ,
.IR Templates/ ,
.IR Backups/ ,
and
.IR config.lock .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Accepted for diagnostics. Human output remains stable.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show help for the selected command, or general help when no command is given.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
With no command, print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "create [template] [options]"
Create a file by copying the selected template to a destination folder. The
default base name is the app setting
.BR defaultBaseName " (default: Untitled),"
not the template display name. The extension comes from the template file.
With no template reference, the configured default template is used. If no
default is configured and several templates exist, the command fails with an
ambiguous-reference error.
.TP
.B create options
.BR \-\-name ", " \-n " base"
Set the base name without the template extension.
.TP
.BR \-\-output ", " \-o " path"
Set the full destination path. Overrides
.B \-\-dir
and
.BR \-\-name .
.TP
.BR \-\-dir ", " \-d " folder"
Set the destination folder. The default is the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-unique
Fail when the destination exists instead of adding a numeric suffix.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-app\-location
Use the configured default folder when one is set; otherwise use the current
directory.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the created file.
.TP
.B \-\-reveal
Reveal the created file in Finder.
.TP
.B \-\-sound
Play the completion sound.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the destination that would be used without creating a file.
.TP
.BI "\-\-template " reference
Use
.I reference
instead of a positional template argument.
.TP
.BR "list [options]" " or " "ls"
List templates. By default all templates, including disabled ones, are shown.
.TP
.B list options
.B \-\-favorites
Only favorites.
.TP
.B \-\-enabled
Only enabled templates.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " name"
Only templates in the named category.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Accepted; this is the default.
.TP
.BI "show [template]" " or " "info"
Print the template ID, file name, display name, category, extension, enabled
and favorite state, use count, dates, and absolute file path.
.TP
.BI "add " "file..." " [options]"
Copy files, packages, or folders into the Templates folder and add template
metadata. Existing template files are not overwritten; a unique file name is
used when needed.
.TP
.B add options
.BI \-\-name " display-name"
Set the display name when exactly one file is added.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " name"
Set the category. When omitted, the category is inferred from the extension.
.TP
.B \-\-favorite
Mark the added templates as favorites.
.TP
.B \-\-disabled
Add the templates disabled. They do not appear in menus.
.TP
.BI "remove " "template" " [options]" " or " "rm"
Remove a template from the configuration and move its file to Trash. If the
removed template was the default, the first remaining template becomes the
default.
.TP
.B remove options
.B \-\-keep\-file
Leave the template file in the Templates folder. The library no longer
references it.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Skip the interactive confirmation. Required when standard input is not a
terminal.
.TP
.BI "favorite [template] [\-\-on|\-\-off]" " or " "fav"
Toggle the favorite flag when neither flag is given. Passing both flags is a
usage error.
.TP
.BI "enable " template
Enable a template.
.TP
.BI "disable " template
Disable a template. Its file is kept.
.TP
.BI "recent [\-\-limit " count "]"
List recently used templates, most recent first. The default limit is 5.
.TP
.BR categories " or " cats
List categories present in the library and their template counts.
.TP
.B config
.B config path
prints the active configuration path.
.B config export [path|\-]
writes pretty-printed JSON; use
.B \-
or omit
.I path
for standard output.
.B config import path
replaces the configuration from a JSON file; template files are not imported.
.B config reset \-\-yes
restores default settings. Template files are kept on disk but are no longer
referenced by the reset library.
.TP
.B status
Print the version, configuration path, template counts, default name, app
running state, Finder extension state, login-item status, shortcut, and CLI
links.
.TP
.BI "open [template]"
Open a template file in its default application. With no argument, open the
Templates folder in Finder.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the support directory, configuration, schema, template files, duplicate
names and IDs, app installation, Finder extension registration, and CLI links.
A failed check makes the command exit with status 1.
.TP
.BI "completion " "zsh|bash"
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
.BI "help [command]"
Print general or command-specific help.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B import\-legacy
Hidden development helper that imports templates and settings from known
legacy support locations. Normal installations do not need it.
.SH TEMPLATE REFERENCES
A template can be referenced by:
.IP 1. 4
Full UUID.
.IP 2. 4
Exact display name, file name, or file name without extension,
case-insensitively.
.IP 3. 4
Normalized name with spaces and punctuation ignored.
.IP 4. 4
Unique case-insensitive prefix.
.PP
An omitted reference uses the default template. If there is no default and
exactly one template exists, that template is used.
.SH OUTPUT
Human-readable data is written to standard output. Warnings and errors are
written to standard error.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-json ,
standard output contains one envelope:
.PP
.nf
{ "ok": true, "command": "create", "data": { ... } }
.fi
.PP
On failure:
.PP
.nf
{ "ok": false, "command": "create",
  "error": { "code": "not_found", "message": "...",
             "exitCode": 3, "suggestions": [ ... ] } }
.fi
.PP
JSON keys and error codes are locale-independent. Human output is English in
version 2.0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error, or a failed
.B doctor
check.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or a destructive command without confirmation in a
non-interactive session.
.TP
.B 3
Template or file not found.
.TP
.B 4
Ambiguous template reference.
.TP
.B 5
Conflict, such as
.B \-\-no\-unique
with an existing destination.
.TP
.B 6
Configuration error: corrupt file, unsupported schema, or write failure.
.TP
.B 7
Permission error: unwritable destination, unreadable template, or invalid
destination.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NFC_SUPPORT_DIR
Absolute path to an alternate support folder. Intended for tests and isolated
automation.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the default support folder and CLI links.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/config.json
Settings, templates, recents, and revision.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/Templates/
Template files.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/config.json.bak
Previous configuration written by the store.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/config.lock
Interprocess lock used by writers.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/Backups/
Quarantined corrupt configurations.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/New File Creation 2/logs/
Local diagnostic log.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a text file in the current directory:
.PP
.nf
nfc create "Text File"
.fi
.PP
Create a named Python file:
.PP
.nf
nfc create "Python Script" \-\-name report
.fi
.PP
Create in a specific folder and reveal the result:
.PP
.nf
nfc create "HTML Page" \-\-dir ~/Documents \-\-reveal
.fi
.PP
Find the next free name without creating a file:
.PP
.nf
nfc create "Text File" \-\-dry\-run \-\-quiet
.fi
.PP
Add a file as a favorite template:
.PP
.nf
nfc add ~/notes.md \-\-category Documents \-\-favorite
.fi
.PP
Export the configuration:
.PP
.nf
nfc config export ~/Desktop/nfc-config.json
.fi
.PP
Use an isolated support folder:
.PP
.nf
NFC_SUPPORT_DIR=/tmp/nfc-test nfc list
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
New File Creation 2 documentation:
.I docs/CLI.md
and
.I docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
in the source distribution.
.PP
The app Help menu opens the bundled README.
.SH NOTES
.B nfc
makes no network requests and has no accounts, analytics, or telemetry.
Template file contents are copied byte-for-byte.
